    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) combined with long-term memory offers a compelling solution to this problem. By building a Personal Knowledge OS, you can create an AI assistant that doesn't just store your information but actively helps you rediscover, synthesize, and reason about it. Unlike generic large language models that hallucinate or provide generic answers, a properly implemented RAG system grounds its responses in your actual documents, providing citations and maintaining strict privacy controls. This article explores how to architect and build such a system, covering everything from document ingestion and vector embeddings to memory management and production deployment considerations."
